    "final_answer": "From the Oyez page for Brown v. Board of Education of Topeka (1) (https://www.oyez.org/cases/1940-1955/347us483), the recorded information is as follows:\n\n- Docket number: 1\n- Deciding Court: Warren Court\n- Argued dates: December 9–11, 1952\n- Reargued dates: December 7–9, 1953\n- Decided date: May 17, 1954\n\nQuestion (from the Question section on the Brown I page):\n- \"Does the segregation of public education based solely on race violate the Equal Protection Clause of the Fourteenth Amendment?\"\n\nDecision information (from the Conclusion decision card on the Brown I page):\n- Decision split: Unanimous decision\n- Prevailing side: for Brown et al.\n- Majority-opinion author: Earl Warren (\"majority opinion by Earl Warren\")\n- One-line holding (the single-sentence holding immediately below the majority-opinion label on the Conclusion card, not the longer explanatory paragraph):\n  - \"Separate but equal educational facilities for racial minorities is inherently unequal violating the Equal Protection Clause of the Fourteenth Amendment.\"\n\nAll requested identity, date, question, and decision fields have been captured from the specified Brown v. Board of Education of Topeka (1) page on Oyez, keeping argued and reargued date ranges distinct and using the Conclusion card for the decision fields and one-line holding.",
